preConditionHook:
// A SHARP LEG IMMEDIATELY ANSWERED BY AN ALMOST EQUALLY SHARP LEG THE OTHER
// WAY -- Grimes (G05-24): a very high probability of an extended, low-edge
// consolidation, so block new entries. Expected use is NEGATED; the corpus
// states every "do not trade while X" claim positively and lets the
// per-placement negate toggle give the block.
//
// SIDES ARE IDENTICAL TEXT. A two-legged stall is a CONTEXT, not a direction,
// and the pattern is symmetric by construction, since the two legs point
// opposite ways whichever came first.
//
// THE TWO LEGS ARE THE THREE NEWEST ALTERNATING PIVOTS, and there are exactly
// two ways they can lie, distinguished by which series carries the NEWEST
// pivot. Bars-ago counts, so the older anchor carries the LARGER count:
//   caseA, a swing pivot low newest (loB2 > hiB1 > loB1): the first leg ran UP
//     from loPx2 to hiPx1 and the second ran DOWN from hiPx1 to loPx1;
//   caseB, a swing pivot high newest (hiB2 > loB1 > hiB1): the first leg ran
//     DOWN from hiPx2 to loPx1 and the second ran UP from loPx1 to hiPx1.
// The two are mutually exclusive, so at most one is taken. In BOTH cases the
// second leg is hiPx1 - loPx1, the span between the two newest pivots, and its
// duration is the gap between their bar indices.
//
// THE OPPOSITE SIGNS ARE STRUCTURAL, not tested: consecutive legs between
// alternating pivots necessarily point opposite ways, so the merged
// pseudocode's sign(leg1) != sign(leg2) is satisfied by the ordering guard and
// the two legs are measured as POSITIVE magnitudes. Both are required positive
// all the same, which is what makes the similarity band meaningful.
//
// THE SIMILARITY BAND IS AGAINST THE LARGER LEG, the looser of the two
// readings, and the larger is picked with a plain comparison rather than
// MaxList -- MaxList's register row scopes it to tick-grid PRICE operands and
// these are computed differences, so the explicit if-form is used in both
// twins. Grimes gives no number; 0.25 is the miner's. maxLegBars bounds the
// SECOND leg's duration, which is what "immediately answered" means.
//
// NOT SpikeReversedBySpike, the BAR-RUN form, which carries no magnitude
// comparison. Not OppositeLargeBarsInWindow, which needs only one large bar of
// each sign anywhere in a window. Not ExpandingTrianglePattern, which needs
// BOTH series diverging over five pivots. The pivot prices read here are the
// same A/B/C anchors LegOneEqualsLegTwoTarget reads, and its ordering guard is
// the one copied.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED, mirroring the twin's Occurrence 1 and 2 reads.
// MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot
// test is MIXED -- AT OR BEYOND the swingStrength OLDER bars, STRICTLY BEYOND
// the swingStrength NEWER bars, and bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER index
// the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the k < j loop; the confirmation lag is
// exactly swingStrength bars, so j starts there; pivotLookback is EL's Length
// with offsets 0..pivotLookback-1 inclusive while the neighbourhood test
// reaches swingStrength bars PAST the window, so the deepest index touched is
// pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength; an empty window is the -1 SENTINEL,
// guarded on the BAR INDEX and never on a price; the comparisons carry the
// 2.22e-12 relational tolerance. Occurrence 3+ is UNMEASURED and never asked
// for. The low side's tie sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule.
// No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs. AbsValue is ACCEPTED and
// std::fabs is its counterpart; <cmath> is already included by the emitter.
//
// Written WITHOUT break and with the < 2 counters, statement for statement
// with the twin's Occurrence 1 / 2 reads. Every scratch value that must
// survive the bar is a localVariables entry rather than a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength.
pivS = (int)swingStrength;
pivW = (int)pivotLookback;
nHi = 0;
nLo = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiB1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiB2 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loB1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
for (int j = pivS; j <= pivW - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - pivS; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivS; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHi < 2) {
        nHi = nHi + 1;
        if (nHi == 1) { hiPx1 = high[j]; hiB1 = (double)j; }
        if (nHi == 2) { hiPx2 = high[j]; hiB2 = (double)j; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLo < 2) {
        nLo = nLo + 1;
        if (nLo == 1) { loPx1 = low[j]; loB1 = (double)j; }
        if (nLo == 2) { loPx2 = low[j]; loB2 = (double)j; }
    }
}
caseA = (loB1 != -1.0) && (loB2 != -1.0) && (hiB1 != -1.0)
    && el_gt(loB2, hiB1) && el_gt(hiB1, loB1);
caseB = (hiB1 != -1.0) && (hiB2 != -1.0) && (loB1 != -1.0)
    && el_gt(hiB2, loB1) && el_gt(loB1, hiB1);
legPrev = 0.0;
legLast = 0.0;
legBars = 0.0;
if (caseA) {
    legPrev = hiPx1 - loPx2;
    legLast = hiPx1 - loPx1;
    legBars = hiB1 - loB1;
}
if (caseB) {
    legPrev = hiPx2 - loPx1;
    legLast = hiPx1 - loPx1;
    legBars = loB1 - hiB1;
}
bigLeg = legPrev;
if (el_gt(legLast, legPrev)) bigLeg = legLast;
similar = (caseA || caseB) && el_gt(legPrev, 0.0) && el_gt(legLast, 0.0)
    && el_lt(std::fabs(legLast - legPrev), similarityFraction * bigLeg)
    && el_le(legBars, maxLegBars);
